{"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PrivacyPolicy","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"PrivacyPolicy","symbolKind":"struct","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PrivacyPolicy","kind":"identifier"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK13PrivacyPolicyV"},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/PrivacyPolicy\/init(deletionGracePeriodDays:)","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/PrivacyPolicy\/init(from:)"],"title":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/PrivacyPolicy\/deletionGracePeriodDays"],"title":"Instance Properties"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/PrivacyPolicy\/encode(to:)"],"title":"Instance Methods"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PrivacyPolicy","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/privacypolicy"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK"]]},"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/PrivacyPolicy","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Data-retention rules that apply after a subject asks to be erased."}],"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/Se","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/SE","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/s8SendableP"],"title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships"}],"references":{"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The official Swift SDK for AXIAM (Access eXtended Identity and Authorization Management)."}],"title":"AxiamSDK"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/PrivacyPolicy/deletionGracePeriodDays":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"deletionGracePeriodDays"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"}],"title":"deletionGracePeriodDays","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/PrivacyPolicy\/deletionGracePeriodDays","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/privacypolicy\/deletiongraceperioddays","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How long a requested account erasure stays cancellable before the purge runs, in days."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The window exists so an erasure triggered by mistake, or under coercion, can be undone —"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"POST \/api\/v1\/auth\/account\/delete\/cancel"},{"type":"text","text":" works for exactly this long. It was fixed at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"30 days in the handler, which meant the “cancel a pending deletion” control in the admin"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"UI referred to a duration no operator could see or change. Shorter is the more"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"restrictive direction, so a tenant may lower it and not raise it: it is time spent"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"holding data the subject has already asked to have erased, and GDPR Art. 17(1) asks for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that to be “without undue delay”. The upper bound of 90 days is where Art. 12(3)’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one-month response deadline plus its two-month extension for complex cases runs out;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"anything past 30 wants a reason recorded."}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentat